---
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400.css';
import '@fontsource/instrument-serif/400-italic.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/500.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-sans/600.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/500.css';
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import GrindCalibrator from '../../components/coffee/GrindCalibrator.svelte';
import grinderData from '../../data/grinders.json';

const title = 'Grind Calibrator: Your Grinder’s Own Settings, Method by Method';
const description = 'Pick your grinder and brew method and see the setting or range its maker publishes (for two grinders, a labelled secondary source), on your grinder’s own dial: Baratza, Fellow, Comandante, 1Zpresso, Niche, Breville and more, each with its source.';
const grinders = grinderData.grinders;
const longDate = (iso: string) => new Date(`${iso}T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' });
const secondary = grinders.filter((g) => g.settings.some((s) => s.provenance !== 'maker')).map((g) => g.short);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
		<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="JayArr Coffee: Deep Brew research" href="/deep-brew/rss.xml" />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
			'@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'Grind Calibrator', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee/deep-brew/calibrator/', description,
			applicationCategory: 'UtilityApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'JayArr Coffee', url: 'https://jayarr.coffee' },
		})}></script>
	</head>
	<body class="cf-page db-dark">
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="cf-intro">
				<a href="/deep-brew/" class="cf-back">← Deep Brew</a>
				<p class="cf-kicker">Deep Brew · Grind Calibrator</p>
				<h1>Your grinder's own <em>starting setting</em></h1>
				<p class="cf-lede">Choose your grinder and how you brew. It shows the setting or range its maker publishes for that method, in the maker's own numbers, with the chart it came from. For the two grinders with no maker chart we could find, it uses a documented secondary source and says so.</p>
			</section>
			<section class="cf-tool" aria-label="Grind Calibrator"><GrindCalibrator client:load /></section>

			<article class="cf-body">
				<h2>Why every grinder needs its own number</h2>
				<p>A grind setting is a position on one grinder's dial, not a size. "15" on a Baratza Encore, 15 clicks on a Comandante and 15 on a 1Zpresso JX-Pro are three different things, because each grinder's burrs, steps and zero point differ. So the calibrator never converts one grinder's number into another's. It shows what each maker publishes for its own grinder, in that grinder's unit.</p>
				<p>Some makers print one setting per method; others print a range. Where there's only a range, the tool shows the band on the dial and doesn't invent a single number inside it.</p>

				<h2>A starting point, then taste</h2>
				<p>Makers present these as starting points, and the coffee decides the rest: the beans, the roast, how fresh they are and your recipe all move the right setting. Brew at the starting setting, taste, then move in small steps. Sour or thin usually means go finer; bitter or harsh usually means go coarser. The <a href="/tools/fix-my-coffee/">Coffee Doctor</a> helps you tell which, and the <a href="/tools/grind-guide/">Grind Guide</a> shows what the grounds should look like.</p>

				<h2>Where zero is</h2>
				<p>Hand grinders count clicks or numbers from a zero point, and makers define zero differently: some count from where the handle starts to turn with resistance, others from where the burrs just touch. The calibrator shows each maker's own definition under "Where zero is". If your count starts somewhere else, the published settings will be off by that difference. A few makers also say how far one click moves the burrs (12.5 µm on a JX-Pro, for example). That is the burr movement, not the size of the grounds.</p>

				<h2>The grinders</h2>
				<p>{grinders.length} grinders, from the makers' own charts and manuals, checked on {longDate(grinderData.checked)}. {secondary.length ? `For the ${secondary.join(' and ')}, no maker chart could be found, so the settings come from a documented secondary source and are labelled that way.` : ''} {grinderData.excluded.length ? `Not included yet: ${grinderData.excluded.map((e) => e.name).join(', ')}, because no maker chart for that exact model could be verified.` : ''}</p>
				{[['electric', 'Electric grinders'], ['hand', 'Hand grinders']].map(([type, label]) => (
					<>
						<h3>{label}</h3>
						<ul class="cf-cols">
							{grinders.filter((g) => g.type === type).map((g) => <li><a href={`/deep-brew/calibrator/?grinder=${g.id}`}>{g.short}</a></li>)}
						</ul>
					</>
				))}

				<h2>Sources</h2>
				<ul class="cf-sources">
					<li>Each grinder maker's own grind chart, manual or published recipe, linked beside every setting in the tool, checked {grinderData.checked}.</li>
					<li>Documented secondary sources, only where no maker chart could be verified, labelled in the tool.</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>.cf-page { background: var(--t-paper, #f3ede3); }</style>
<style>
	main { color: var(--t-ink, #2a1d15); }
	.cf-intro { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 22px; }
	.cf-back { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-ink-3, #75655a); text-decoration: none; }
	.cf-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--t-crema-deep, #8f5d22); margin: 26px 0 0; }
	h1 { font: 400 clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px)/.98 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 10px 0 12px; }
	h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--t-coffee, #7a4e30); }
	.cf-lede { font: 400 17px/1.5 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--t-ink-2, #5b4a3d); max-width: 62ch; margin: 0; }
	.cf-tool { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 8px 24px 40px; }
	.cf-body { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 24px 72px; font: 400 17px/1.7 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, sans-serif; }
	.cf-body h2 { font: 400 34px/1.1 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; margin: 44px 0 12px; }
	.cf-body a { color: var(--t-coffee, #7a4e30); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
	.cf-cols { columns: 2; column-gap: 24px; padding-left: 18px; }
	.cf-sources { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--t-ink-2, #5b4a3d); }
	@media (max-width: 640px) { .cf-intro { padding: 96px 16px 18px; } .cf-tool { padding: 4px 12px 32px; } .cf-body { padding: 16px 16px 56px; } .cf-cols { columns: 1; } }
</style>
